UID:6189-1790854200-1790859600@hurthub.davidson.edu
SUMMARY:AI\, Systems\, and the Future of Brand Building
DESCRIPTION:Lunch and learn with Jennifer Kattula\, GM & CMO of Microsoft Advertising\, on real-world AI adoption and what leaders should know.\n\n\nAI transformation is not a technology problem. It is a people\, systems and workflow problem. That is the point of view Jennifer Kattula brings to the table as General Manager and Chief Marketing Officer of Microsoft Advertising\, where she leads global marketing for one of the world’s largest ad platforms. \nJennifer is joining the Hurt Hub for a lunch and learn on what it takes to build AI systems that hold up as models and solutions keep changing underneath them. Grab lunch and pull up a chair for a candid\, hour-long conversation. \nShe’ll cover: \n\nHer experience leading AI transformation from inside Microsoft\nWhat she’s hearing directly from CMOs and other C-suite leaders about real-world AI adoption\nHow organizations should build AI systems flexible enough to survive rapid change in models and tools\nThe questions every leader should be asking about governance\, data\, confidentiality\, enterprise versus personal accounts\, and first-party information\n\n \nAbout Jennifer \nAn engineer by training\, a builder by instinct\, and a connector at heart\, Jennifer brings a rare combination of technical mastery and brand craft to marketing’s most pivotal moment today\, when leaders forging brand endurance must be as fluent in systems as they are in stories. \nJennifer’s 20+ year career spans transformative roles at PwC\, Sapient\, American Express\, and 11 years at Meta\, where she was Global Head of Platforms Marketing. She also led marketing at Web3 startup Polygon Labs. \nJennifer is a recognized thought leader on generative AI in advertising. She speaks and writes about the future of brand-building in an AI-native world\, helping business leaders find the balance between technology and humanity\, and honor both. \nJennifer holds a B.S. in Chemical Engineering and an MBA from the University of Michigan. \n \nThis is a featured program of the Applied AI Lab at the Hurt Hub at Davidson College \nAccess and exposure to innovation for all is our vision\, and that includes access to the people shaping how AI is actually being adopted inside the world’s biggest companies. This conversation is sponsored by the Applied AI Lab and is open to students\, faculty\, staff\, alumni\, entrepreneurs\, and the Greater Charlotte community. \n——————————————————————- \nThe Hurt Hub welcomes requests for reasonable accommodations related to disability and will strive to make this program accessible to participants. Please contact our team at the Hurt Hub at contact@example.edu to make such a request.
URL:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/event/ai-systems-and-the-future-of-brand-building/
LOCATION:The Hurt Hub at Davidson College\, 210 Delburg Street\, Davidson\, NC 28036\, Davidson\, NC\, 28036\, US
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/6189_image-1.png
END:VEVENT
