UID:4301-1791282600-1791284400@hurthub.davidson.edu
SUMMARY:Keith Kleeman '97 Alumni Innovator-in-Residence Office Hours
DESCRIPTION:Have an idea you can’t stop thinking about? A problem you want to solve? Drop in and talk it through with Keith Kleeman ’97\, the Hurt Hub’s Alumni Innovator-in-Residence. \nKeith is a serial biotech entrepreneur who has spent more than two decades building companies at the intersection of science\, writing and technology. He founded Medical Communication Consultants and grew it to 400 writers supporting the approval of more than 25 therapeutics\, created ClinGenuity\, one of the pharmaceutical industry’s earliest AI platforms\, and today leads Celvant and Optimvia. His path started at Davidson as a biology major writing a novel on the side\, and it has never fit neatly in one box. \nYou don’t need a business plan or a startup to stop by. Keith believes innovation is a mindset\, not a job title: seeing what could be better and asking\, “How do I fix this?” Bring a question\, an early idea\, a venture in progress or just your curiosity. \nOpen to Davidson students\, faculty\, staff and alums\, Hurt Hub coworking members and entrepreneurs across the Charlotte region. \nKeith will be hosting the office hours in the Innovation Lab at the Hurt Hub. You can also schedule virtual office hours with him but need to indicate that when you register. \nThis listing covers Keith’s October 6 time slots\, but he’s hosting office hours on several dates this month: October 6\, 7\, 15\, 16\, 21\, 23\, 27\, and 28. Use the registration link to sign up for any session that works for you.
URL:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/event/keith-kleeman-97-final-innovator-in-residence-office-hours/
CATEGORIES:Free for Students,Hybrid,Office Hours
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/keith-kleeman-headshot-scaled.jpeg
END:VEVENT
