UID:6268-1791460800-1791464400@hurthub.davidson.edu
SUMMARY:Process: Your GPS to Sales Repeatability
DESCRIPTION:Learn a practical way to think about sales process design and a simple framework to begin applying immediately\n\n\nJoin us at the Hurt Hub for a Lunch & Learn on Sales Process! \nNewer firms sometimes neglect to define a formal sales process. Yet scaling requires a clear\, customer-aligned approach that helps teams operate with greater efficiency and effectiveness\, resulting in stronger win rates\, market share gains\, and more reliable sales outcomes. \nParticipants will leave with a practical way to think about sales process design and a simple framework they can begin applying immediately to their own customer journey. \nWho Should Attend: Founders of start-ups and early-stage firms who want to implement a repeatable\, revenue-producing sales process. A structured process helps the organization deliver consistent results and creates a foundation for scalable growth. \nLearning Objectives \n1. Recognize why a repeatable sales process is one of the most important growth assets an early-stage company can build — creating order\, consistency\, scalability\, forecast accuracy\, and revenue predictability. \n2. Learn how customers make buying decisions and how to position yourself as the guide they trust to reach their desired outcome. \n3. Apply a simple framework to begin mapping your own sales process — aligning marketing\, sales\, and customer success around the way your customers make buying decisions. \nAbout the Presenter: \nJohn W. Buckner brings a broad sales and growth background from a thirty-year corporate career\, including leadership roles as vice president of marketing and senior vice president of sales. His experience spans Fortune 500 companies\, strong middle-market national firms\, OEMs\, restaurant chains\, convenience retail\, and major retailers\, including organizations such as Dupont\, Georgia-Pacific\, Simpson Strong Tie\, Chick-fil-A\, Taco Bell\, Sonic\, 7-Eleven\, Walmart\, Target\, Home Depot\, and Lowe’s. \nHis firm\, Insightful Selling\, helps small businesses win through people\, process\, and technology. John holds degrees in education\, psychology\, counseling psychology\, and business administration\, including an executive MBA. \n \nThe Hurt Hub welcomes requests for reasonable accommodations related to disability and will strive to make this program accessible to participants. Please contact our team at the Hurt Hub at contact@example.edu to make such a request.
URL:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/event/process-your-gps-to-sales-repeatability/
LOCATION:The Hurt Hub at Davidson College\, 210 Delburg Street\, Davidson\, NC 28036\, Davidson\, NC\, 28036\, US
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/6268_image.png
END:VEVENT
