UID:5485-1792584000-1792587600@hurthub.davidson.edu
SUMMARY:Innovation Community of Practice
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Hurt Hub’s monthly Innovation Community of Practice! \nFAQ \nWhat is a Community of Practice? \nA community of practice (CoP) is a group of people who share a common interest\, profession\, or passion and come together to interact\, learn\, and collaborate. \nWhat do we mean by Innovation? \nWe like to explore innovation broadly. We’re curious about new ideas\, methods\, or services that bring positive change or improvement. We want to explore creative approaches to problem-solving\, processes\, idea generation\, or technology.  \nWho is this group for? \nInnovation is for everyone regardless of industry or professional status. We welcome curious individuals from all backgrounds. \nWhat will we do? \nThese are casual conversations that focus on a different topic month to month. Generally\, a volunteer facilitator will share briefly about a topic they’re interested in and then open up the floor for the group to discuss.  \nWhat Topics have your covered?  \nPatterns & Intersections\, Vibe Coding\, Art and AI\, Travel\, Circular Economies\, Ideation Techniques\, Mental Models\, Innovation & Spirituality\, Storytelling through collage. \nIs food served? \nSorry not at this one! Participants are welcome to bring their own lunch. \nFor questions or to RSVP please email Event Contact  \contact@example.edu \nThe Hurt Hub welcomes requests for reasonable accommodations related to disability and will strive to make this program accessible to participants. Please contact Event Contact at contact@example.edu to make such a request.
URL:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/event/innovation-community-of-practice-2/
CATEGORIES:Discussion,Social
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hurthub.davidson.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_1426.jpg
END:VEVENT
